  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9ca80317-ae25-519d-8c38-297f5a42be69" activityNameId="746dcc33-6d2e-535b-bc76-7d1b0de66187" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Ethanol, 95% in H2O, from sugar beet molasses, at distillery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Ethanol, 95% in H2O, from sugar beet molasses, at distillery
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg hydrated ethanol 95% (dry basis, i.e. 1.05 kg hydrated ethanol 95% wet basis), respectively 1 kg of stillage syrup (wet basis) from molasses. The multioutput-process 'sugar beet molasses, in distillery' delivers the co-products 'ethanol, 95% in H2O, from sugar beet molasses, at distillery' and 'syrup, from sugar beet molasses, at distillery'. Economic allocation with allocation factor for common stages of 94.5% to ethanol. Allocation is done according to carbon balance for CO2 emissions.;
UUID: 1273d235-9fa6-320f-87a9-2abd93448855
This dataset includes the transport of molasses to the distillery, and the processing of molasses to hydrated ethanol (95%) and molasses stillage syrup (58% dry matter). System boundary is at the distillery. Dehydration to anhydrous ethanol is not included.
Location: Data is from the etha+ project (Alcosuisse, CH)
Technology: The process is similar to that of sugarbeet-to-ethanol. The production of syrup from stillage includes pre-concentration and concentration. The syrup is 58% dry matter and is used as animal feed.
Time period: Data from 1998 to 2005, current technology for the production of ethanol from sugar-based feedstocks
Production volume: Production volume of ethanol for use as a fuel was 1-1.5 Ml in 2005 in CH
Sampling: Data is from the etha+ project (Alcosuisse, CH), technology by French ethanol plant supplier, modelling by ENERS (CH) 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1273d235-9fa6-320f-87a9-2abd93448855.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
